 "brief": {
  "short_answer": "When the control/link is lost, standard procedures favor attempting to reestablish link, then executing pre-set loss-of-link actions (RTH, hover, or land) per the device\u2019s failsafe settings. FAA guidance emphasizes attempting to reestablish the control link and, if not possible, to start emergency procedures. DJI manuals describe configurable loss-of-link actions (RTH, hover, or land) with RTH paths shown when possible, and potential additional failsafe modes if vision systems or GNSS are unavailable.",
  "sections": [
   {
    "section": "faa",
    "label": "FAA guidance",
    "status": "drafted",
    "abstain_reason": null,
    "claims": [
     {
      "text": "If the control link is lost, try to reestablish the connection and, if it cannot be reestablished, start emergency or contingency procedures for loss of control link.",
      "citations": [
       "faa_ac_107_2a_2022_c0228",
       "faa_ac_107_2a_2022_c0227"
      ],
      "quote": "start emergency or contingency procedures for loss of control link.",
      "conditions": [],
      "assessment": "supported",
      "claim_id": "C001",
      "section": "faa",
      "tier": "official",
      "incident_label": null
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "section": "manual:DJI Matrice 30T",
    "label": "DJI Matrice 30T manual",
    "status": "drafted",
    "abstain_reason": null,
    "claims": [
     {
      "text": "The aircraft\u2019s loss-of-signal behavior is configurable; the action can be set to RTH, land, or hover.",
      "citations": [
       "manual:DJI Matrice 30T:dji_m30t_manual_v22_c0032",
       "manual:DJI Matrice 30T:dji_m30t_manual_v22_c0033"
